<title>SWEDEN: Sandvik sees small gain from Custos sale.</title>
<headline>Sandvik sees small gain from Custos sale.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish tools and speciality metals maker Sandvik said on Friday that it would get a small capital gain from the sale of its 1.8 million A-shares in Swedish investment company Custos.  </p>
<p>&quot;Sandvik has sold its entire stake of shares in Custos, or approximately 1.8 million A-series shares. The sale results in a small capital gain for Sandvik,&quot; Sandvik said in a statement.</p>
<p>No other details were given.</p>
<p>Sandvik said earlier it intended to sell the stake.</p>
<p>At 1240 GMT Custos was eight crowns higher at 135 crowns. Sandvik was down 0.50 crown at 158.50.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom, +46-8-700 1017</p>
